/* Main computational kernel. The whole function will be timed,
   including the call and return.

   Optimized implementation:
   -------------------------
   We compute, for all i,j:

       C[i,j] = beta * C[i,j] + alpha * sum_k A[i,k] * B[k,j]

   using a three-level blocked algorithm over (i, j, k) and a small
   temporary tile of C kept in fast memory.

   High-level structure per (I,J) tile of C (I: i-block, J: j-block):

     1) Load a GEMM_BLOCK_I x GEMM_BLOCK_J tile of C into C_tile and
        apply the beta scaling once:
             C_tile = beta * C_tile;

     2) For each K-block of the reduction dimension:
          accumulate alpha * A * B into C_tile:
             C_tile += alpha * A_block * B_block;

     3) Write the updated tile back to C.

   This improves:
     - Data locality for C (each element loaded/stored once),
     - Locality and reuse for A and B within tiles,
     - SIMD vectorization along the j (column) dimension.
